  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 246 AM MDT SAT OCT 3 2026\nThe upper level ridge will rebuild across the area after Monday,\nkeeping temperatures 10 to 20 degrees above normal through the \nweek and within a few degrees of record highs in many locations.\nWinds will be light through Thursday with mostly clear skies. \nAn upper level trough will approach the Pacific Northwest on \nFriday and move inland over the weekend. Significant differences\nin the timing and strength of the trough exist between the \nensembles, but the forecast favors cooler temperatures by \nSaturday. Winds will become breezy Friday and Saturday with a \n10 to 20% chance of showers in the central Idaho mountains.",
